# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# uv-managed daemon venv (uv.lock is tracked; the env itself is regenerated by `uv sync --frozen`)
.venv/

# Secrets (email/OAuth/SMTP/SMS/Telegram/calls/Discord/Signal/Google) — never commit
# Every *.env file is ignored globally, so a new secret env file is ignored by default rather than
# by remembering to add a per-name line. Only the tracked *.env.example templates ship.
*.env
**/notion-mcp.json
**/slack-mcp.json
**/*.secret
# HAR captures hold live session cookies/tokens — never commit them
**/*.har
.env
.env.*
!*.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# cockpit/web (Vite + TS + React) — node_modules + build output are regenerated, never tracked.
cockpit/web/node_modules/
cockpit/web/dist/

# cockpit/server — the real archon registry is per-install (seed from the tracked
# archon-registry.example.json); everything else the server writes lives under the already-ignored
# seneschal/state/ (cockpit-audit.jsonl, cockpit-session-secret, cockpit-inbox.jsonl, and the
# break-glass supervisor's breakglass-audit.jsonl + breakglass-assertion-secret). The zitadel
# stack's secrets (cockpit/zitadel/.env) are covered by the `.env` rule above; its postgres data
# lives in a named Docker volume, never in the repo.
cockpit/server/archon-registry.json

# Persona & identity — generated by the setup wizard; contain the owner's personal
# details on a real install. Only the tracked defaults/templates/examples ship.
persona/persona.md
persona/identity.json
persona/owner-profile.md

# Store — per-machine backend selection + registries filled with real workspace ids
seneschal/store/config.json
seneschal/store/notion/schema.md
seneschal/store/notion/mcp.json

# References — per-install owner data kept beside its tracked *.example.json (the entries name the
# owner's own topics, vendors, accounts and reminder vocabulary). See seneschal/references/CLAUDE.md.
seneschal/references/watch-suppressions.json
seneschal/references/reminder-aliases.json
# The Telegram topic routing table (purpose -> topic title); telegram_topics.py falls back to the
# tracked telegram-topics.example.json when it is absent. Runtime thread ids live in state/.
seneschal/references/telegram-topics.json

# Archons (Forge mode) — generated scaffolds, run outputs, runtime state, and
# per-archon private inputs (profile, watchlist, voice profile) stay local; only
# *.example.*, state/README.md, and tools are tracked. Each archon also carries its
# own .gitignore (the layout rule in seneschal/references/archons.md); these root
# rules are the safety net for archons that lack one.
archons/scaffolds/
archons/need/
archons/stable/
# `out/*` rather than `out/`: git never descends into an excluded *directory*, so a re-include of a
# tracked README inside one would be silently ignored. Only an out/README.md is ever tracked —
# deliverables carry the owner's data.
archons/*/out/*
!archons/*/out/README.md
archons/*/state/*
!archons/*/state/README.md
!archons/*/state/*.example.json
!archons/*/state/*.example.jsonl
!archons/*/state/*.example.md
archons/*/profile.json
archons/*/watchlist.json
archons/*/voice-profile.md

# Runtime state — local-first, regenerated; track only docs + examples.
# The runtime memory logs (state/run-log.md, state/carry-over.md,
# state/standing-safety.json, state/brief-prestage.json, state/open-loops.json) live here so the daemon can run off main without pull
# conflicts on files the assistant rewrites at runtime; the active store is the
# system of record. So do the background-job records and their bookkeeping (state/jobs/,
# state/job-pushes/, state/session-mail/, state/current-turn.json, state/pending-checks.jsonl,
# state/owi-*). A job's --worktree checkout lives OUTSIDE the repo (a sibling
# `seneschal-worktrees/` dir, or $SENESCHAL_WORKTREE_ROOT), so it never needs a rule here.
# See seneschal/state/README.md.
seneschal/state/*
!seneschal/state/README.md
!seneschal/state/*.example.json
!seneschal/state/*.example.jsonl
!seneschal/state/*.example.md
